window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-7be3f970bd43699c"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"computer-use\">电脑操作（Computer Use）</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code> 可获取对应 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>在支持的地区，ChatGPT 桌面应用中的 Computer Use 可在 macOS 和 Windows 上配合 ChatGPT Work 与 Codex 使用。请安装 Computer Use 插件。在 macOS 上，如果系统提示，请授予“屏幕录制”和“辅助功能”权限。</p> <p>借助 Computer Use，ChatGPT 可以查看并操作 macOS 或 Windows 的图形用户界面。适用于命令行工具或结构化集成无法满足需求的任务，例如检查桌面应用、使用浏览器、更改应用设置、处理尚无插件支持的数据源，或复现仅在图形界面中出现的错误。</p> <p>由于 Computer Use 可能影响项目工作区之外的应用和系统状态，请将任务范围限定清楚，并在继续之前检查权限提示。</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-computer-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"computer-use_1\">设置 Computer Use</h2> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，在切换器里选择 ChatGPT 并切换到 Work，或直接选择 Codex。打开 <strong>插件（Plugins）&gt; Computer Use</strong>；如果出现提示，请选择<strong>安装插件（Install plugin）</strong>。如果 ChatGPT 显示<strong>启用（Enable）</strong>，请先启用它。打开 Computer Use 服务器和技能的开关，然后选择<strong>立即试用（Try now）</strong>开始。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：Computer Use 插件控制项，其中 MCP 服务器和技能均已启用</p> </blockquote> <p>然后打开<strong>设置（Settings）&gt; 电脑操作（Computer use）</strong>，检查应用访问权限。已连接的浏览器控制项会显示<strong>管理（Manage）</strong>操作。你批准在未来任务中使用的应用会显示在<strong>始终允许的应用（Always-allowed apps）</strong>区域。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：Computer Use 设置中的应用控制项；计算器是唯一始终允许的应用</p> </blockquote> <p>在 Windows 上，任务运行期间，请让目标应用保持显示在当前活动桌面上。在 macOS 上，如果系统提示，请授予“屏幕录制”和“辅助功能”权限，以便 ChatGPT 查看并操作目标应用。</p> <p>在 macOS 上，请授予：</p> <ul> <li><strong>屏幕录制</strong>权限，让 ChatGPT 能查看目标应用。</li> <li><strong>辅助功能</strong>权限，让 ChatGPT 能点击、输入和导航。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"when-to-use-computer-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"computer-use_2\">何时使用 Computer Use</h2> <p>对于依赖截图或视觉判断的困难任务，如果模型选择器中提供了<a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6-astra\">GPT-6 Astra</a>，可以选择它。插件设置、操作系统权限和应用访问控制的要求仍然相同。</p> <p>当任务依赖难以仅通过文件或命令输出验证的图形界面时，适合使用 Computer Use。</p> <p>适用场景包括：</p> <ul> <li>测试 ChatGPT 正在构建的 macOS 应用、Windows 应用、iOS 模拟器流程或其他桌面应用。</li> <li>执行需要使用网页浏览器的任务。</li> <li>复现仅在图形界面中出现的错误。</li> <li>更改需要通过图形界面逐步点击才能完成的应用设置。</li> <li>检查插件尚不可用的应用或数据源中的信息。</li> <li>在 macOS 上，当你继续处理其他工作时，在后台执行范围明确的任务。</li> <li>执行跨越多个应用的工作流。</li> </ul> <p>对于你正在本地开发的 Web 应用，请优先使用<a href=\"#/article/a-a7de5b39bd26a809\">内置浏览器</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"windows-foreground-use\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"windows\">Windows 前台操作</h3> <p>在 Windows 上，Computer Use 会在当前活动桌面中运行。你继续使用同一个 Windows 会话时，它无法在后台操作，因此任务运行期间，ChatGPT 可能会移动指针、输入文字并占用前台。</p> <p>如果希望离开电脑后 Windows 任务仍继续，请让设备保持解锁并连接互联网。你可以通过手机上的<a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f\">远程控制</a>查看进度或发送后续指令；也可以在 Windows 虚拟机中运行 ChatGPT 桌面应用，让 Computer Use 接管虚拟机，而不是你的主桌面。</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-computer-use-task\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"computer-use_3\">开始 Computer Use 任务</h2> <p>在提示中提及 <code>@Computer</code> 或 <code>@AppName</code>，或直接要求 ChatGPT 使用 Computer Use。请明确说明 ChatGPT 应操作的应用、窗口或流程。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Open the app with Computer Use, reproduce the onboarding bug, and fix the\nsmallest code path that causes it. After each change, run the same UI flow\nagain.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请使用 Computer Use 打开应用，复现新用户引导中的缺陷，并修复导致该问题的最小代码路径。每次修改后，都重新运行同一套界面流程。</div></div> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Open @Chrome and verify the checkout page still works after the latest changes.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">打开 @Chrome，验证最新更改后结账页是否仍然正常工作。</div></div> <p>如果目标应用提供专用插件或 MCP 服务器，请优先使用结构化集成来访问数据并执行可重复的操作。当 ChatGPT 需要通过视觉来检查或操作应用时，再选择 Computer Use。</p> <p><a id=\"permissions-and-approvals\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">权限和审批</h2> <p>工作区管理员可以限制 Computer Use 可访问的应用，以及是否允许保存审批决定。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=control-browser-and-computer-use\">托管浏览器和 Computer Use 控制项</a>。</p> <p>Computer Use 的系统权限与 ChatGPT 中的应用审批彼此独立。在 macOS 上，“屏幕录制”和“辅助功能”权限允许 ChatGPT 查看并操作应用；应用审批则决定你允许 ChatGPT 使用哪些应用。文件读取、文件编辑和 Shell 命令仍遵循该任务的沙箱和审批设置。</p> <p>使用 Computer Use 时，ChatGPT 只能查看并操作你允许使用的应用。执行任务期间，ChatGPT 会先请求你授权使用电脑上的应用。你可以选择<strong>始终允许（Always allow）</strong>，这样以后 ChatGPT 使用该应用时便无需再次询问。要移除应用，请在 ChatGPT 桌面应用的设置中的 <strong>Computer Use</strong> 区域，打开<strong>始终允许（Always allow）</strong>列表进行删除。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：Computer Use 请求访问计算器的审批对话框</p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT 也可能在执行敏感或会造成明显影响的操作之前请求许可。</p> <p>如果 ChatGPT 无法查看或控制应用，请打开<strong>系统设置（System Settings）&gt; 隐私与安全性（Privacy &amp; Security）</strong>，在 macOS 上检查 <strong>Codex Computer Use</strong> 的“屏幕录制”和“辅助功能”权限。在 Windows 上，请确认目标应用显示在当前活动桌面中。</p> <p><a id=\"windows\"></a> <strong>配置 Windows 应用策略</strong></p> <p>在 Windows 上，Computer Use 会将持续生效的应用决定保存在 <code>$CODEX_HOME/config.toml</code> 中。列出 Computer Use 无需询问即可打开的应用：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[computer_use.windows]\nalways_allowed_app_ids = [\"mspaint.exe\"]\n</code></pre> <p>请使用 Windows Computer Use 报告的应用标识符，例如桌面应用的可执行文件名，或打包应用的应用用户模型 ID。对于未列入清单的应用，ChatGPT 会请求许可。要撤销已保存的决定，请从<strong>设置（Settings）&gt; Computer Use &gt; 始终允许（Always allow）</strong>中移除该应用。</p> <p>此表保存的是本地 Computer Use 决定，与管理员强制执行的 <code>requirements.toml</code> 分开；管理员可以在该文件中使用 <code>[features].computer_use = false</code> 禁用 Computer Use。旧版 <code>$CODEX_HOME/computer-use/config.toml</code> 中的允许清单条目会迁移到当前设置；其中的 <code>denied</code> 列表不属于当前策略架构。</p> <p><a id=\"locked-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">锁定状态下使用</h2> <p>锁定状态下使用功能仅适用于 macOS。在 Windows 上，Computer Use 只能在前台运行。</p> <p>启用后，即使 Mac 已锁定，ChatGPT 也可以使用 Computer Use。适合在 Mac 锁定后，通过已连接的设备执行需要使用桌面应用的 ChatGPT 任务。</p> <p>启用此功能时，ChatGPT 会安装一个参与 macOS 解锁流程的 Apple<a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/security/authorization-plug-ins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">授权插件（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>该功能的适用范围经过刻意限制：它不是通用的 Mac 远程解锁方式，也不会允许其他应用或本地进程解锁电脑。</p> <p>要使用锁定状态下的 Computer Use：</p> <ol> <li>在应用中打开<strong>设置（Settings）&gt; Computer Use</strong>。</li> <li>启用锁定状态下使用。</li> <li>Mac 屏幕锁定后，从已连接的设备启动一个使用 Computer Use 的任务。</li> </ol> <p>Mac 锁定后，如果 ChatGPT 任务通过 Computer Use 访问应用，ChatGPT 会暂时解锁 Mac，同时阻止本地操作，并保留锁定屏幕的保护措施。解锁之前，ChatGPT 会检查解锁请求是否来自一个处于活动状态且可信的 Computer Use 轮次。超出这一短暂的有效时间后，ChatGPT 会拒绝解锁；如有需要，会要求你手动解锁。</p> <p>锁定状态下使用功能包含以下安全措施：</p> <ul> <li>授权窗口有效时间很短，并且仅适用于当前解锁请求。</li> <li>只有 ChatGPT 在 Computer Use 任务执行期间可以自动解锁。</li> <li>桌面暂时解锁期间，ChatGPT 会遮挡每个显示器的画面。</li> <li>如果 ChatGPT 检测到本地键盘或指针输入，会重新锁定 Mac，并暂停自动解锁，直到你手动解锁。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"safety-guidance\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">安全建议</h2> <p>使用 Computer Use 时，ChatGPT 可以查看屏幕内容、截取屏幕截图，并与目标应用中的窗口、菜单、键盘输入和剪贴板状态交互。请把屏幕上可见的应用内容、网页、截图，以及目标应用中打开的文件，视为 ChatGPT 在任务期间可能会处理的上下文。</p> <p>请将任务范围限定清楚；遇到敏感操作流程时，请留在电脑旁：</p> <ul> <li>每次只指定一个明确的目标应用或操作流程。</li> <li>你可以随时停止任务或接管电脑。</li> <li>除非任务确实需要，否则请关闭敏感应用。</li> <li>在 Windows 上，任务运行时 Computer Use 会占用前台输入；你可以改用另一台设备或虚拟机，也可以先停止任务，再使用当前桌面。</li> <li>除非你在场并能逐项批准，否则避免执行需要使用密钥的任务。</li> <li>允许 ChatGPT 使用应用之前，请先检查应用权限提示。</li> <li>只有对 ChatGPT 自动使用该应用感到放心时，才选择<strong>始终允许（Always allow）</strong>。</li> <li>涉及账户、安全、隐私、网络、付款或凭据设置时，请留在电脑旁。</li> <li>如果 ChatGPT 开始操作错误的窗口，请取消任务。</li> </ul> <p>如果 ChatGPT 使用你的浏览器，它可以与已经登录的网页交互。请像亲自操作一样审查网站上的操作：网页可能包含恶意或误导性内容；网站也可能把已批准的点击、表单提交和登录状态下的操作视为由你的账户发起。若你还要继续使用自己的浏览器，请让 ChatGPT 改用另一个浏览器。</p> <p>此功能不能自动化终端应用或 ChatGPT 本身，因为自动化这些对象可能绕过 ChatGPT 的安全策略。它也不能以管理员身份进行身份验证，或代你批准安全和隐私权限提示。</p> <p>在适用的场景中，文件编辑和 Shell 命令仍遵循 ChatGPT 的审批和沙箱设置。通过桌面应用进行的更改，在保存到磁盘并由项目跟踪之前，可能不会显示在审查窗格中。ChatGPT 数据控制也适用于通过 ChatGPT 处理的内容，包括 Computer Use 截取的屏幕截图。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"computer-use\">Computer Use</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>In supported regions, Computer Use in the ChatGPT desktop app is available on macOS and Windows with ChatGPT Work and Codex. Install the Computer Use plugin. On macOS, grant Screen Recording and Accessibility permissions when prompted.</p> <p>With Computer Use, ChatGPT can see and operate graphical user interfaces on macOS or Windows. Use it for tasks where command-line tools or structured integrations aren't enough, such as checking a desktop app, using a browser, changing app settings, working with a data source that isn't available as a plugin, or reproducing a bug that only happens in a graphical user interface.</p> <p>Because Computer Use can affect app and system state outside your project workspace, use it for scoped tasks and review permission prompts before continuing.</p> <h2 id=\"set-up-computer-use\">Set up Computer Use</h2> <p>In the ChatGPT desktop app, select ChatGPT and switch to Work in the switcher, or select Codex. Open <strong>Plugins &gt; Computer Use</strong> and select <strong>Install plugin</strong> if prompted. If ChatGPT shows <strong>Enable</strong>, select it. Turn on the Computer Use server and skill toggles, then select <strong>Try now</strong> to start.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Computer Use plugin controls with the MCP server and skill enabled.</p> </blockquote> <p>Then open <strong>Settings &gt; Computer use</strong> to review app access. Connected browser controls show a <strong>Manage</strong> action. Apps you approve for future tasks appear in the <strong>Always-allowed apps</strong> section.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Computer Use settings showing app controls and Calculator as the only always-allowed app.</p> </blockquote> <p>On Windows, keep the target app visible on the active desktop while the task runs. On macOS, grant Screen Recording and Accessibility permissions when prompted so ChatGPT can see and interact with the target app.</p> <p>On macOS, grant:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Screen Recording</strong> permission so ChatGPT can see the target app.</li> <li><strong>Accessibility</strong> permission so ChatGPT can click, type, and navigate.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"when-to-use-computer-use\">When to use Computer Use</h2> <p>For difficult tasks that depend on screenshots or visual judgment, choose <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6-astra\">GPT-6 Astra</a> when it is available in your model selector. The same plugin setup, operating-system permissions, and app access controls apply.</p> <p>Choose Computer Use when the task depends on a graphical user interface that's hard to verify through files or command output alone.</p> <p>Good fits include:</p> <ul> <li>Testing a macOS app, Windows app, iOS simulator flow, or another desktop app that ChatGPT is building.</li> <li>Performing a task that requires your web browser.</li> <li>Reproducing a bug that only appears in a graphical interface.</li> <li>Changing app settings that require clicking through a UI.</li> <li>Inspecting information in an app or data source that isn't available through a plugin.</li> <li>On macOS, running a scoped task in the background while you keep working elsewhere.</li> <li>Executing a workflow that spans more than one app.</li> </ul> <p>For web apps you are building locally, use the <a href=\"#/article/a-a7de5b39bd26a809\">built-in browser</a> first.</p> <h3 id=\"windows-foreground-use\">Windows foreground use</h3> <p>On Windows, Computer Use runs on the active desktop. It can't operate in the background while you keep using the same Windows session, so expect ChatGPT to move the pointer, type, and take over the foreground while the task runs.</p> <p>For Windows tasks that should continue while you step away, keep the Windows device unlocked and connected to the internet. Use <a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f\">remote control</a> from your phone to check progress or send follow-up instructions, or run the ChatGPT desktop app inside a Windows virtual machine so Computer Use takes over the VM instead of your main desktop.</p> <h2 id=\"start-a-computer-use-task\">Start a Computer Use task</h2> <p>Mention <code>@Computer</code> or <code>@AppName</code> in your prompt, or ask ChatGPT to use Computer Use. Describe the exact app, window, or flow ChatGPT should operate.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Open the app with Computer Use, reproduce the onboarding bug, and fix the\nsmallest code path that causes it. After each change, run the same UI flow\nagain.\n</code></pre> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Open @Chrome and verify the checkout page still works after the latest changes.\n</code></pre> <p>If the target app exposes a dedicated plugin or MCP server, prefer that structured integration for data access and repeatable operations. Choose Computer Use when ChatGPT needs to inspect or operate the app visually.</p> <h2 id=\"permissions-and-approvals\">Permissions and approvals</h2> <p>Workspace administrators can restrict which apps Computer Use can access and whether approvals can be saved. See <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=control-browser-and-computer-use\">managed browser and Computer Use controls</a>.</p> <p>System permissions for Computer Use are separate from app approvals in ChatGPT. On macOS, Screen Recording and Accessibility permissions let ChatGPT see and operate apps. App approvals determine which apps you allow ChatGPT to use. File reads, file edits, and shell commands still follow the sandbox and approval settings for the task.</p> <p>With Computer Use, ChatGPT can see and take action only in the apps you allow. During a task, ChatGPT asks for your permission before it can use an app on your computer. You can choose <strong>Always allow</strong> so ChatGPT can use that app in the future without asking again. You can remove apps from the <strong>Always allow</strong> list in the <strong>Computer Use</strong> section of the ChatGPT desktop app settings.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Computer Use approval dialog requesting access to Calculator</p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT may also ask for permission before taking sensitive or disruptive actions.</p> <p>If ChatGPT can't see or control an app, open <strong>System Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security</strong> and check <strong>Screen Recording</strong> and <strong>Accessibility</strong> for <strong>Codex Computer Use</strong> on macOS. On Windows, make sure the target app is visible in the active desktop session.</p> <p><a id=\"configure-windows-app-policy\"></a> <strong>Configure Windows app policy</strong></p> <p>On Windows, Computer Use stores persistent app decisions in <code>$CODEX_HOME/config.toml</code>. List the apps that Computer Use can open without prompting:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[computer_use.windows]\nalways_allowed_app_ids = [\"mspaint.exe\"]\n</code></pre> <p>Use the app identifier that Windows Computer Use reports, such as an executable name for a desktop app or an app user model ID for a packaged app. ChatGPT prompts for apps that aren't in the list. To revoke a saved decision, remove the app from <strong>Settings &gt; Computer Use &gt; Always allow</strong>.</p> <p>This table stores local Computer Use decisions. It's separate from the admin-enforced <code>requirements.toml</code>, where administrators can disable Computer Use with <code>[features].computer_use = false</code>. Older <code>$CODEX_HOME/computer-use/config.toml</code> allow-list entries are migrated into the current setting; its <code>denied</code> list isn't part of the current policy schema.</p> <h2 id=\"locked-use\">Locked use</h2> <p>Locked use is for macOS. On Windows, Computer Use works in the foreground.</p> <p>Locked use lets ChatGPT use Computer Use after your Mac locks, but only after you enable it. Use it when a ChatGPT task needs to use desktop apps from a connected device after the Mac locks.</p> <p>When you enable locked use, ChatGPT installs an Apple <a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/security/authorization-plug-ins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">authorization plug-in (online)</a> that participates in the macOS unlock flow.</p> <p>Locked use is intentionally narrow. It's not a general-purpose remote-unlock path for your Mac, and it doesn't let other apps or local processes unlock the computer.</p> <p>To use locked use:</p> <ol> <li>Open <strong>Settings &gt; Computer Use</strong> in the app.</li> <li>Enable locked use.</li> <li>Start a task that uses Computer Use from a connected device after your Mac's screen has locked.</li> </ol> <p>When a ChatGPT task accesses an app via Computer Use after your Mac locks, ChatGPT temporarily unlocks the Mac while blocking local use and preserving the locked screen protections. Before unlocking, ChatGPT checks whether the unlock attempt is for an active, trusted Computer Use turn. Outside that short-lived window, ChatGPT denies the unlock and asks you to unlock manually if needed.</p> <p>Locked use includes safeguards:</p> <ul> <li>The authorization window is short-lived and scoped to the current unlock attempt.</li> <li>Automatic unlock is available only to ChatGPT during active Computer Use turns.</li> <li>ChatGPT covers every display while the desktop is temporarily unlocked.</li> <li>If ChatGPT detects local keyboard or pointer input, it relocks the Mac and pauses automatic unlock until you unlock it manually.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"safety-guidance\">Safety guidance</h2> <p>With Computer Use, ChatGPT can view screen content, take screenshots, and interact with windows, menus, keyboard input, and clipboard state in the target app. Treat visible app content, browser pages, screenshots, and files opened in the target app as context ChatGPT may process while the task runs.</p> <p>Keep tasks narrow and stay present for sensitive flows:</p> <ul> <li>Give ChatGPT one clear target app or flow at a time.</li> <li>You can stop the task or take over your computer at any time.</li> <li>Keep sensitive apps closed unless they're required for the task.</li> <li>On Windows, expect ChatGPT to take over foreground input while it works; use a secondary device, a VM, or stop the task before using that desktop yourself.</li> <li>Avoid tasks that require secrets unless you're present and can approve each step.</li> <li>Review app permission prompts before allowing ChatGPT to use an app.</li> <li>Use <strong>Always allow</strong> only for apps you trust ChatGPT to use automatically in future tasks.</li> <li>Stay present for account, security, privacy, network, payment, or credential-related settings.</li> <li>Cancel the task if ChatGPT starts interacting with the wrong window.</li> </ul> <p>If ChatGPT uses your browser, it can interact with pages where you're already signed in. Review website actions as if you were taking them yourself: web pages can contain malicious or misleading content, and sites may treat approved clicks, form submissions, and signed-in actions as coming from your account. To keep using your browser while ChatGPT works, ask ChatGPT to use a different browser.</p> <p>The feature can't automate terminal apps or ChatGPT itself, since automating them could bypass ChatGPT security policies. It also can't authenticate as an administrator or approve security and privacy permission prompts on your computer.</p> <p>File edits and shell commands still follow ChatGPT approval and sandbox settings where applicable. Changes made through desktop apps may not appear in the review pane until they're saved to disk and tracked by the project. Your ChatGPT data controls apply to content processed through ChatGPT, including screenshots taken by Computer Use.</p>"};
